<% content_for :title, "Users" %>

<%# 013 User Story 2: who is registered on this site, and who was first.
    Read-only by design (FR-009) — there is no control here, because there is no
    capability behind one: administrator status is claimed once at signup and
    never granted or revoked by hand. %>
<div class="stack">
  <div id="admin-user-directory" class="card stack-tight">
    <h1 class="page-title">Registered users</h1>

    <%# 012 FR-005: a table above the breakpoint, one labelled card per account
        below it, from the same markup rendered once — so both forms show the
        same accounts in the same order, because there is only one order.

        The explicit roles are what keep that safe: changing an element's display
        drops the implicit table roles, and a screen reader has to meet each
        account as a set of labelled fields either way (012 FR-005d). %>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="data-table" role="table">
        <thead>
          <tr role="row">
            <th scope="col" role="columnheader">Email</th>
            <th scope="col" role="columnheader">Joined</th>
            <%# FR-012: its own column rather than a mark tacked onto the email,
                so the one row that differs says how it differs. %>
            <th scope="col" role="columnheader">Role</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>

        <tbody>
          <% @users.each do |user| %>
            <tr id="admin-user-row-<%= user.id %>" role="row">
              <td class="strong" role="cell" data-label="Email"><%= user.email %></td>
              <td class="meta" role="cell" data-label="Joined"><%= l user.created_at, format: :long %></td>

              <%# 008 FR-025: the tint decorates the word, it does not replace it —
                  "Admin" is what carries the meaning, for a reader who cannot
                  tell the badge's colour from any other. %>
              <td role="cell" data-label="Role" class="<%= "detail-value-empty" unless user.admin? %>">
                <% if user.admin? %>
                  <span class="badge badge-info">Admin</span>
                <% else %>
                  —
                <% end %>
              </td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
